{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The thigh of the terumah and the breast of the tenufah</b> — in the language of \"אֲשֶׁר הוּנַף וַאֲשֶׁר הוּרָם\" (Exodus 29:27). Tenufah — moving back and forth; terumah — raising up and bringing down. And why the verse divided them, terumah for the thigh and tenufah for the breast, we do not know, for both of them involve lifting and waving. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 10:15). And what appears correct to me for the reason of this is that during the ordination offerings the thigh was a terumah to YHWH, and it was burned together with the bread and with the fats. And the elevated portion from the shelamim is called terumah, as it says (Leviticus 7:14): \"And he shall present from it one from every offering as a terumah to YHWH.\" All the more so these, which they raised upward, for they are all terumah to YHWH. And it is not called by the name tenufah, because its waving was together with the fats and the bread in order to burn them to YHWH. But the breast was waved on its own, and it was not distinguished from the rest of the meat except through the waving, and through this waving alone it was consecrated, and Moses merited through it for it to be his portion. And because the privilege of Aaron and his sons in the breast and the thigh for all generations was from the day of ordination, and they merited the thigh through its terumah to YHWH and the breast through its tenufah, and the rest of the meat belonged to the owners, it shall forever be called the thigh of terumah and the breast of tenufah, as it was regarding them on the day of the privilege." "<b>Upon the fires of the fats</b> — like \"upon the fats of the fires.\" From here we learn that the fats are below at the time of waving. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 10:15). But there is no need for this, for \"fires of\" (אִשֵּׁי) is an epithet for the fats, as it says (Deuteronomy 18:1): \"the fires of YHWH and His inheritance they shall eat.\" And the interpretation of this verse is that it is the reason for what He said (Leviticus 10:14): \"for it is your portion and the portion of your sons, given from the sacrifices of the peace offerings of the children of Israel,\" and He said: the thigh of the terumah and the breast of the tenufah upon the fires of the fats — the children of Israel who are mentioned shall bring them to wave a tenufah before YHWH, so that they shall be consecrated before Him, and they shall be for you and your sons as an eternal statute. For the command regarding the tenufah — this is not its place, but according to our method we learn from it that the fats are below at the time of waving."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Ramban first cites Rashi's admission that the reason for the different terms is unknown, then offers his own explanation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:52:26.754067046Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}